WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:34.649
That was Volcan, live, answering in its own voice. It is a Model Context Protocol server built to be called by Alexa+, so a blind or low-vision developer can review an AI agent's pull request by voice, and hear the verdict first.

2
00:00:34.649 --> 00:01:13.027
This patch, an inverted admin check, goes to Claude on Amazon Bedrock. Volcan runs on AWS Lambda, with its review state in Amazon DynamoDB.

3
00:01:13.027 --> 00:01:24.132
The meter names Amazon Bedrock, this line says how much of the patch the model read, and this panel opens its full answer.

4
00:01:24.132 --> 00:01:46.963
Back on the pull request, request changes stages a review, bound to the head commit Volcan read. Listen.

5
00:01:46.963 --> 00:02:21.568
Nothing leaves until you confirm, and this build has no GitHub token, so it records the review and sends nothing. Confirm, and listen.

6
00:02:21.568 --> 00:02:34.036
This handshake is a real one with the server under the page, at protocol revision 2025-11-25. Alexa+ itself has never called Volcan.
